  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Key Takeaway.</strong> AXP rewarded patient capital with a ~250x price multiple and consistent dividend income, but only investors who could withstand multiple 40%+ drawdowns — including a near-84% peak-to-trough collapse in 2008–09 — captured the full long-term return. The stock's annualized volatility of {a['kpis']['annualized_volatility']:.1f}% reflects significant risk concentration, in line with its identity as a cyclically exposed financial services franchise.
