</header>

<main>

<section id="exec-summary">
  <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
  <p>From its split-adjusted opening close of <strong>${a['kpis']['first_close']:.4f}</strong> on {a['period']['start']} to a closing price of <strong>${a['kpis']['last_close']:.2f}</strong> on {a['period']['end']}, American Express has delivered a cumulative price return of <strong>{a['kpis']['cumulative_return']:,.1f}%</strong> across {a['period']['years']:.1f} years — equivalent to a compounded annual growth rate (CAGR) of <strong>{a['kpis']['cagr']:.2f}%</strong>. This performance was achieved through extreme cyclical volatility, including a peak-to-trough drawdown of <strong>{a['kpis']['max_drawdown']:.1f}%</strong> during the 2007–2009 Global Financial Crisis, the deepest in the dataset.</p>

  <p>The current price of <strong>${a['kpis']['last_close']:.2f}</strong> sits <strong>{(a['kpis']['last_close']/a['extremes']['ath_price']-1)*100:.1f}%</strong> below the all-time high of <strong>${a['extremes']['ath_price']:.2f}</strong> recorded on {a['extremes']['ath_date']}. Over the full dataset, AXP distributed <strong>${a['kpis']['total_dividends']:.2f}</strong> in cumulative per-share dividends, paid across {a['dividend_events_count']} discrete events.</p>

  <h3>Headline KPI Dashboard</h3>
  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi positive">
      <div class="label">Cumulative Return</div>
