<section id="decade">
  <h2>5. Decade-by-Decade Performance Comparison</h2>
  <p>Comparing AXP across discrete decades exposes how the macroeconomic regime shaped shareholder outcomes. The 1980s and 1990s delivered roughly 20% annualized growth amid disinflation and financial-sector tailwinds; the 2000s were a "lost decade" (zero CAGR) bracketed by the dot-com unwind and the GFC; the 2010s and 2020s rebuilt long-term compounding alongside rising dividend distributions.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Decade</th><th class="num">Start → End Price</th><th class="num">Total Return</th><th class="num">CAGR</th><th class="num">Ann. Volatility</th><th class="num">Max Drawdown</th><th class="num">Dividends Paid</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>'''

for d in a['decades']:
    ret_cls = 'pos' if d['total_return'] > 0 else 'neg'
    cagr_cls = 'pos' if d['cagr'] > 0 else 'neg'
    html += f'''<tr>
      <td><strong>{d['name']}</strong></td>
      <td class="num">${d['start_price']:.2f} → ${d['end_price']:,.2f}</td>
      <td class="num {ret_cls}">{d['total_return']:+,.1f}%</td>
      <td class="num {cagr_cls}">{d['cagr']:+.2f}%</td>
      <td class="num">{d['volatility']:.2f}%</td>
      <td class="num neg">{d['max_drawdown']:.1f}%</td>
      <td class="num">${d['dividends']:.2f}</td>
    </tr>'''

html += f'''
